#42983
A Large House~
   All of the houses in Chisha appears to have been created by the same
architect due to their simple and like design.  They include two large rooms: a
living area with a kitchen and a bedroom.  The house is barely decorated, with
a modest table, chairs and stove serving as the kitchen.  The living area, in
the same room as the kitchen, has a large couch opposite the window.  The
bedroom area has a medium sized bed on the long wall and a small desk in the
corner of the room.  Upon the walls are the Chishan symbol which seems to have
been burned into it.    
~
429 12 0 0 0 0 255 0
